{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "02", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "20", "M": "40", "S": "58"}}, "news": [{"title": "After Mumbai pilot, micro-zoning for property rates to reach Thane, Navi Mumbai", "para": "Maharashtra will extend its micro-zoning property valuation system to Thane and Navi Mumbai. This reform replaces uniform Ready Reckoner rates with development-based valuations. A pilot survey is underway in Mumbai, which will inform the rollout. The new system aims for more transparent and equitable property valuations. This initiative will benefit middle-class homebuyers and slum residents across the state.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/maharashtra-expands-micro-zoning-for-property-valuation-to-thane-and-navi-mumbai/132812418?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-398458/132812418.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Maharashtra plans land titling law, property cards for all owners", "para": "Maharashtra will soon introduce a Land Titling Act for digital property titles. This new law aims to replace existing ownership records with government-backed digital titles. The proposed framework, modeled on Dubai and Singapore, will be placed before the legislature. A mandatory measurement policy will precede property registration, streamlining transactions. Individual vertical property cards will be issued to urban cooperative housing society owners.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/maharashtra-to-introduce-landmark-land-titling-law-with-digital-property-cards/132812353?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-123358/132812353.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Nagpur civic body collects \u20b9100 crore in property tax in four months", "para": "Nagpur Municipal Corporation has collected over Rs100 crore in property tax by July 30. This collection represents a significant portion of the annual demand, driven by early payment rebates. Taxpayers received incentives for online and timely payments, encouraging prompt tax submission. Several zones contributed substantially, with Laxmi Nagar leading the revenue generation efforts. The civic body continues recovery measures and technology use for improved tax compliance.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/nagpur-municipal-corporation-surpasses-100-crore-in-property-tax-collections-amid-deadline-rush/132812279?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-566727/132812279.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}